*.pth
*.pt
*.h5
__pycache__/
*.npy
*.json
# ...but spec/ artefacts ARE the project record and must be committed.
#
# The blanket *.json above exists to keep dataset labels and embeddings out of the
# repo -- a job the data/ and work/ rules below already do by directory. As written
# it also swallowed spec/2026-09-08-osie-eval-baseline/paper_reference.json, the
# hand-transcribed published row that the generated run record depends on. It never
# appeared as untracked, so the file simply was not there on the next checkout: an
# ignore rule that hides a file you meant to commit fails exactly the way D7 says
# nothing should. Negated rather than narrowed, so any future spec JSON is safe too.
!spec/**/*.json
# ...and so are the SE-Net configs: SE-Net/configs/*.json are hparam SOURCE files,
# not data. The tracked ones (osie/coco) predate the blanket *.json rule and stayed
# tracked because .gitignore does not untrack; a NEW one -- eve_useremb.json, F3's --
# would have been silently ignored, the same failure the spec/ negation above records.
!SE-Net/configs/*.json
# Subject-level gaze data and staged dataset artefacts (TechStack 6.5).
# data/ holds osie_fixations_update_duration.json, the COCO fixation labels and
# the per-dataset embeddings.npy -- none of it belongs in the repo.
data/
work/
logs/

# MSDeformAttn compiler output (F3 Step 3: `sh SE-Net/src/pixel_decoder/ops/make.sh`).
# This is the one step that writes into SE-Net/, and it must be visibly a build
# artefact rather than an edit to a tracked file.
*.so
**/ops/build/
*.egg-info/
